We can keep this as a cautionary implication: $\text{love as pursuit or means}
\longrightarrow
\text{desire or pleasure}
\longrightarrow
\text{division}.$ The arrow does not mean a theorem. It preserves the lecture’s warning: when love is made into something to be acquired, used, or fulfilled, it has already entered the field of pleasure and division.

